{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ses_a4985715f0b3fMfe4enf8z3es7","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"call_ccb221653da7ffeee8911c6f","status":"completed","title":"/workspace/notes.md","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"# Build cache notes\n\nThe CI job restores its dependency cache from a key made of the runner image and the branch name.\nWhen the lockfile changes the key stays the same, so the restored store no longer matches it and\nthe install step refuses it. Rebuilding by hand fixes one run, then the next lockfile change breaks it again.\n\n## Ideas\n\n- hash the lockfile into the key;\n- keep a restore key without the hash, so most packages still come from the cache;\n- share one store between branches that have the same lockfile.\n\nReviewed: the lockfile hash goes into the cache key."}}],"rawOutput":{"output":"/workspace/notes.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Build cache notes\n2: \n3: The CI job restores its dependency cache from a key made of the runner image and the branch name.\n4: When the lockfile changes the key stays the same, so the restored store no longer matches it and\n5: the install step refuses it. Rebuilding by hand fixes one run, then the next lockfile change breaks it again.\n6: \n7: ## Ideas\n8: \n9: - hash the lockfile into the key;\n10: - keep a restore key without the hash, so most packages still come from the cache;\n11: - share one store between branches that have the same lockfile.\n12: \n13: Reviewed: the lockfile hash goes into the cache key.\n\n(End of file - total 13 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Build cache notes\n\nThe CI job restores its dependency cache from a key made of the runner image and the branch name.\nWhen the lockfile changes the key stays the same, so the restored store no longer matches it and\nthe install step refuses it. Rebuilding by hand fixes one run, then the next lockfile change breaks it again.\n\n## Ideas\n\n- hash the lockfile into the key;\n- keep a restore key without the hash, so most packages still come from the cache;\n- share one store between branches that have the same lockfile.\n\nReviewed: the lockfile hash goes into the cache key.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/notes.md","text":"# Build cache notes\n\nThe CI job restores its dependency cache from a key made of the runner image and the branch name.\nWhen the lockfile changes the key stays the same, so the restored store no longer matches it and\nthe install step refuses it. Rebuilding by hand fixes one run, then the next lockfile change breaks it again.\n\n## Ideas\n\n- hash the lockfile into the key;\n- keep a restore key without the hash, so most packages still come from the cache;\n- share one store between branches that have the same lockfile.\n\nReviewed: the lockfile hash goes into the cache key.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":13,"totalLines":13,"truncated":false}}}}}}
